Subject: [A14 platform 16/18] phy boot mode

Extracted mechanically from Python rewrite 16 in the tested postPatch recipe.
No resulting source changes; existing diagnostics and workarounds are retained.
Apply in the order in kernel/a14-post-patch.nix, after its DT appends.
The existing bank0 patch remains between platform patches 09 and 10.

diff --git a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
--- a/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
+++ b/drivers/phy/qualcomm/phy-qcom-qmp-combo.c
@@ -5234,6 +5234,21 @@
 
 	if (of_property_present(dev->of_node, "mode-switch") ||
 	    of_property_present(dev->of_node, "orientation-switch")) {
+		/*
+		 * A14 boot experiment: USB3DP is the default cached mode, so a
+		 * dock already attached at boot can request USB3DP without
+		 * exercising the mux reconfiguration used after reconnect.
+		 * Start switchable Glymur ports in USB-only mode and let the
+		 * negotiated DP request select the combined or DP-only mode.
+		 * Fixed-wired DP/eDP PHYs keep their data-lanes configuration.
+		 */
+		if (qmp->cfg == &glymur_usb3dpphy_cfg &&
+		    of_property_present(dev->of_node, "mode-switch")) {
+			qmp->qmpphy_mode = QMPPHY_MODE_USB3_ONLY;
+			dev_info(dev,
+				 "A14-BOOT: initial Type-C mode USB3_ONLY; waiting for negotiated DP mux\n");
+		}
+
 		ret = qmp_combo_typec_register(qmp);
 		if (ret)
 			goto err_node_put;
